{
  "_meta": {
    "title": "Restyle video (Wan2.2 Fun VACE)",
    "description": "Core nodes only. The source clip is trimmed from the start to the window (Video Slice, length/16 s), resampled to 16 fps (VideoFrameSample uniform), scaled/cropped to the output size and turned into canny edges, which drive WanVaceToVideo as the control video, so motion and layout follow the source while the prompt sets the look. An optional style reference image (LoadImage -> reference_image) is added by the builder. Two-stage Wan2.2 sampling (8 steps, shift 8): high-noise model without LoRA at cfg 3.5 for steps 0-4 (prompt adherence), low-noise model + lightx2v 4-step LoRA at cfg 1 for steps 4-8. speed=fast puts the high-noise LoRA (node 5) in and runs 4 steps at cfg 1 on both stages. Length 4n+1 frames (<= 81, 5 s), ~480p. Source audio is not carried over."
  },
